#Analysis

Product Service – Initial Analysis

Basic Idea / Project Goal:

The main objective of this project is to implement CRUD operations on the Product domain.
Role-based access control needs to be implemented so that only ADMIN users can create, update, or delete products, whereas normal USER roles can only view the available products.
Buying or ordering functionality is intentionally excluded from this assignment scope following the YAGNI (You Aren’t Gonna Need It) principle.

---

Domain Analysis:

Product Entity:

The Product entity represents the items managed in the system.

Fields required:

* id (Integer) – Primary key for product table
* productName (String) – Name of the product
* productQuantity (Integer) – Quantity available
* availability (Boolean) – Indicates whether the product is available. Since it is a primitive boolean, the default value will be false
* createdAt (DateTime) – Timestamp when the product is created
* modifiedAt (DateTime) – Timestamp when the product is last updated
* createdBy (String) – Stores which user created the product
* modifiedBy (String) – Stores which user modified the product

Assumption: createdBy and modifiedBy fields are required for auditing purposes to track who has added or updated the data in the database.

---

User Entity:

The User entity represents registered users of the system.

Fields required:

* id (Integer) – Primary key for user table
* name (String) – Name of the user
* email (String) – Email address used for login
* contact (String) – Contact number
* role (Enum) – USER or ADMIN
* password (String) – Hashed password stored securely in the database
* createdAt (DateTime) – Timestamp when the user is created
* modifiedAt (DateTime) – Timestamp when the user is last updated

---

Business Logic / System Actions:

* A user can register into the system by providing the required details.
* Registered users can update their own profile information.
* Users can belong to either USER or ADMIN role.
* Separate APIs will be provided for USER and ADMIN functionalities.
* JWT-based authentication will be used to secure the APIs.
* Role-based authorization will ensure that:

  * ADMIN users can create, update, and delete products.
  * USER roles can only view the list of products and product details.

